{"id": "2026-10-05-sports-swiss-nati-win-again-perfect-nine-points", "date": "2026-10-05", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Swiss Nati win again, perfect nine points", "summary": "Switzerland beat Scotland 3-0 and Slovenia 2-1 to lead Nations League B1 with maximum points.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/nations-league/rating-schweiz-slowenien-siegtorschuetze-ndoye-geniesst-die-gunst-der-srf-user", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["football", "nations-league"], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Two further results since the opening 3-0 in North Macedonia: a 3-0 away win in Scotland and a 2-1 win over Slovenia on Sat 2026-10-03, after a shaky start, decided by Nottingham Forest winger Dan Ndoye with a finish while facing away from goal. That makes three wins from three — nine points, the maximum — in a group that also holds Slovenia and Scotland (both on 4 points per the cross-checked standings). The context a non-follower needs: the Nations League (UEFA's national-team league, tiered like a ladder with promotion and relegation) has Switzerland in League B for the first time, so winning the group is the route back up to League A, the top tier.", "why": "Winning the group is the whole point of this campaign, and a perfect start puts Switzerland well clear of Slovenia and Scotland, who have four points each.", "thread_id": "2026-10-05-sports-swiss-nati-win-again-perfect-nine-points", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-05", "event_date": "2026-10-03", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "UEFA Nations League", "Dan Ndoye"]}
{"id": "2026-10-05-sports-gc-hire-janssen-after-sacking-zeidler", "date": "2026-10-05", "stream": "sports", "headline": "GC hire Janssen after sacking Zeidler", "summary": "Grasshoppers appointed Olaf Janssen twelve days after sacking Peter Zeidler; the club sit 10th in the Super League.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/super-league/wieder-ein-deutscher-der-neue-gc-trainer-heisst-olaf-janssen", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["football", "super-league"], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Grasshopper Club Zürich (GC), one of Switzerland's most storied clubs, confirmed Olaf Janssen, 59, on a contract to summer 2027. Janssen was assistant coach at Wolfsburg in the Bundesliga and most recently head coach at fourth-tier Sandhausen until March, so this is not a marquee appointment. The stakes are at the bottom: GC are 10th, two points clear of last-placed Lausanne-Sport, after back-to-back 5-2 and 5-1 defeats under Zeidler (who had only arrived in May and guided the club through the relegation play-off). The league itself paused for the national-team window; as of the last round on 2026-09-20 Lugano led with 25 points, six ahead of Young Boys, and Basel had sacked Stephan Lichtsteiner and hired Slavisa Jokanovic after losing the second game following his departure.", "why": "Two top-flight clubs, Basel and GC, have changed coach within a month; the international break is the cheapest moment to do it, and GC's new man inherits a team that cannot defend (24 goals conceded in nine games).", "thread_id": "2026-10-05-sports-gc-hire-janssen-after-sacking-zeidler", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-05", "event_date": "2026-10-03", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Grasshopper Club Zürich", "Olaf Janssen", "Peter Zeidler"]}
{"id": "2026-10-05-sports-verstappen-wins-chaotic-sepang-race", "date": "2026-10-05", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Verstappen wins chaotic Sepang race", "summary": "Verstappen won the Sepang GP after an FIA software bug delayed the start; Russell retired and Antonelli leads by 84.", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-bahrain-gp-in-malaysia-report/10861849/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["f1"], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Max Verstappen (Red Bull) took his first victory of 2026, ahead of championship leader Kimi Antonelli (Mercedes) and Lewis Hamilton (Ferrari, his first podium since Silverstone). The more important result is for the title: Antonelli's team-mate and closest title rival George Russell, who had started seventh and run second, retired with a power-unit failure while on course for a podium, so Antonelli's lead over him grew to 84 points (320 to 236, from the cross-checked standings) with seven races to go — a win is worth 25. Before a wheel turned in anger, the race was delayed about 90 minutes: after a storm, several cars including Verstappen's and Hamilton's lost throttle response on the formation lap. FIA single-seater director Nikolas Tombazis said the sport had never run the new cars in properly wet conditions and a bug in the engine software stopped power being redeployed when cars crawled; a fix was written and installed before the restart.", "why": "Reliability, not speed, is now the main threat to Antonelli's lead, and the \"unacceptable\" electronics glitch (drivers' word, not the FIA's) is a worry the sport must answer before the next wet race.", "thread_id": "2026-10-05-sports-verstappen-wins-chaotic-sepang-race", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-05", "event_date": "2026-10-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Formula 1", "Max Verstappen", "Kimi Antonelli", "FIA"]}
{"id": "2026-10-05-sports-evans-wins-world-rally-title", "date": "2026-10-05", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Evans wins world rally title", "summary": "Elfyn Evans won the WRC title after Oliver Solberg ran off the road in the final stage.", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/wrc/news/wrc-sardinia-elfyn-evans-claims-historic-title-after-oliver-solberg-crashes-in-final-stage-showdown/10861985/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["wrc"], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Toyota's Elfyn Evans became Britain's first world rally champion since Richard Burns in 2001 after fellow Toyota driver Oliver Solberg ran off the road two corners from the end of the closing Power Stage (a short televised stage that carries bonus points). The two were level on points going into it, with Solberg set to win on countback (the tie-break by wins) if they finished level, so Evans needed to beat him on the stage. Evans, who had punctured and finished the rally only fifth, said he was \"quite sure it was over\". Solberg still won the rally itself — his third win of the year — by 57.6 seconds, but lost the title.", "why": "A championship settled by a single mistake in the very last minutes of the season is the clearest reminder that rallying's points are about the whole weekend, not the event win.", "thread_id": "2026-10-05-sports-evans-wins-world-rally-title", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-05", "event_date": "2026-10-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Elfyn Evans", "Oliver Solberg", "WRC", "Toyota"]}
{"id": "2026-10-05-sports-djokovic-beats-zverev-as-beijing-seeds-fall", "date": "2026-10-05", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Djokovic beats Zverev as Beijing seeds fall", "summary": "Djokovic beat Zverev at the China Open while Sabalenka lost to Bartunkova.", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/tennis/articles/c8kge0d95dzno", "source_domain": "bbc.co.uk", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["tennis"], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Novak Djokovic, 39, beat top seed and world number two Alexander Zverev 4-6 6-4 6-4 to reach the semi-finals (against Daniil Medvedev) and stay unbeaten in Beijing for 32 matches; BBC reports the loss dents Zverev's bid to finish the year as world number one. On the women's side, world number two Aryna Sabalenka lost to 34th-ranked Nikola Bartunkova 6-4 6-3 a day after top seed and world number one Elena Rybakina went out, so for the first time since 2015 neither top seed reached the last 16 — and Rybakina has since withdrawn from the Wuhan Open (12-18 October) with a foot injury.", "why": "Djokovic has no title yet in what he calls a difficult 2026, while the women's top two are leaving the autumn swing open.", "thread_id": "2026-10-05-sports-djokovic-beats-zverev-as-beijing-seeds-fall", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-05", "event_date": "2026-10-04", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Novak Djokovic", "Alexander Zverev", "China Open"]}
